---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/url';
---
<Base title="About Our Reef Gear Research" description="Learn how ReefMetric uses published equipment specs and sizing math to compare reef gear, explain estimates, and help you plan a saltwater tank.">
  <section class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--brand-2)">About</p>
    <h1>We measure reef gear so you don’t have to guess.</h1>
    <p style="font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--muted)">ReefMetric is an independent, reader-supported resource for saltwater aquarium keepers. We pair published manufacturer and retailer specifications with sizing calculations and side-by-side comparisons so you can choose equipment for your actual tank.</p>
    <h2>How we rate</h2>
    <p>Every recommendation starts with the numbers that matter for your tank: skimmer rating vs. bioload, pump flow vs. head loss, PAR vs. depth. Our current comparisons use published specs and calculated estimates. They are not first-hand bench tests. Read <a href={url('/how-we-rate')}>how we rate reef gear</a> to see the methods and limits.</p>
    <h2>How we stay independent</h2>
    <p>Approved affiliate links may earn a commission when you buy, at no extra cost to you. That never changes what we recommend — our rankings are driven by the data, not the payout. <a href={url('/disclosure')}>Read our full disclosure</a>.</p>
    <h2>What the tools help you decide</h2>
    <p>A pump that looks large enough on its box may deliver less water once it has to lift it through your plumbing. The <a href={url('/tools/return-pump-calculator')}>return pump calculator</a> estimates that loss and compares the result with pump curves. The <a href={url('/tools/protein-skimmer-calculator')}>skimmer size calculator</a> adjusts capacity for stocking and lets you check whether the body fits your sump. Both help narrow a buying list; neither can measure conditions inside your own aquarium.</p>
    <p>The <a href={url('/reviews/best-reef-led-lighting')}>reef lighting review</a> shows recorded PAR readings, their test conditions, and gaps in our records. The <a href={url('/tools/reef-build-cost-calculator')}>reef tank cost calculator</a> puts equipment and running expenses in one place so you can see what a build leaves out before you order.</p>
    <h2>How to check a recommendation</h2>
    <p>Start with your tank's water volume, available equipment space, and the coral and fish you plan to keep. Follow the source links beside product data, check the date, and confirm the current model and price with the retailer. A different pump revision, mount height, or sump water level can change the answer. Estimates are starting points, not guarantees of a particular result.</p>
    <p>ReefMetric currently publishes under its site name rather than named individual authors. No individual credentials or personal testing history are claimed here.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
